\section{Counting people who lost their plan}{

Each plan-county appears once, so \code{sum(dec_enrollment)} counts every
December enrollee once. The share of December enrollment that lost
coverage in a year is
\code{sum(dec_enrollment[lost_coverage]) / sum(dec_enrollment)}, and the
\code{outcome} splits that total by type. \code{dec_enrollment_low} gives the
lower bound when CMS-suppressed counts (1-10 enrollees) are counted as 1
instead of 10.

Plan-, contract- and county-level columns (\verb{plan_*}, \code{contract_exits},
\verb{n_plans_*}, \verb{county_*}, 2018 county values, \code{benchmark}) repeat on
every row of their plan or county; the \code{counting} column of
\code{\link[=maexits_catalog]{maexits_catalog()}} flags them.
}

\section{Outcomes}{

A plan-county's enrollees keep coverage when some January plan the
crosswalk links it to serves the county: the same plan renewed
(\code{renewed}, \code{renewed_sae}, \code{renewed_sar_kept_county},
\code{consolidated_same_plan_id}), or another plan of the same or another
contract (\code{moved_plan_same_contract}, \code{moved_contract},
\code{moved_new_plan}). Otherwise they lost it (\code{lost_coverage} TRUE):
\itemize{
\item \code{terminated_contract_listed}, \code{terminated_contract_gone}: the plan
was terminated; split by whether the contract still offers any plan in
January. From the 2024 crosswalk on, CMS labels every termination
"Terminated/Non-renewed Contract" (kept in \code{xwalk_statuses}), so the
split uses the January landscape instead of the label.
\item \code{sar_dropped_county}: the plan continues but dropped this county.
\item \code{moved_plan_not_in_county}, \code{moved_contract_not_in_county},
\code{sar_successor_not_in_county}, \code{new_plan_not_in_county}: enrollees were
moved to a plan that does not serve the county.
\item \code{renewal_not_listed_in_county}: the plan renewed but the January
landscape does not list it in the county. For about 69\% of these
enrollees the plan still reports January enrollment in the county, so
this is the least certain category; drop it through \code{outcome} if
needed.
}

\code{lost_coverage} equals \code{forced_county} in \link{plan_county}, and the
county totals equal the \verb{_once} columns of \link{county_panel}.
}

\section{Coverage gaps}{

Plan details come from \link{plan_details}. The landscape files give no
out-of-pocket maximum for SNPs before CY2025 (\code{moop_in_network} NA),
Part C and Part D star ratings start in CY2024 (plans with Part D only
in CY2024), and D-SNP integration status starts in CY2023. The county
benchmark for the January year is \code{benchmark} on the next \code{dec_year}'s
rows (or in \link{county_panel}). The universe excludes employer group plans,
PACE, Medicare-Medicaid Plans and enrollees living outside a plan's
listed service area (about 3-6\% of CPSC December MA enrollment).
}

